 "title": "4:1 impedance-ratio surface-mount RF transformer, 50 Ω, 2 to 775 MHz",
 "source": {
  "revision": "REV. E",
  "pages": 1
 },
 "summary": "A small surface-mount wideband RF transformer in the six-pad CD542 case. Its secondary presents four times the impedance of its primary, referenced to a 50 Ω system, and the secondary winding has a centre tap brought out to its own pad. Its 3 dB passband runs from 2 to 775 MHz; within the 1 dB band, amplitude balance between the secondary halves is about 0.1 dB and phase balance about 1 degree. Its applications are impedance matching and baluns. The + suffix marks the RoHS-compliant version.",
