 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Winding configuration",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Configuration A: one primary winding between pins 1 and 3 and one secondary winding between pins 4 and 6, with a tap at the secondary's middle on pin 5. The dots on pins 3 and 4 mark the ends that are in phase. The two windings are separate."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Features",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Return loss is typically 20 dB. The part tolerates aqueous washing. It is covered by US patent 6,133,525."
  },
  {
